Defence journalists Shiv Aroor and Rahul Singh have announced that their formal association with Salman Khan’s upcoming film Maatrubhumi, earlier titled Battle of Galwan, has come to an end. In a joint statement released on November 5, the co-authors of the India’s Most Fearless book series said the film has evolved beyond the account of the 2020 Galwan Valley clash featured in their work. The statement read, “Rahul Singh and I (Shiv Aroor) would like to share that our association with Maatrubhumi (earlier titled Battle of Galwan) has come to a close. As the film has evolved, it has moved beyond the account of the Galwan incident in our India’s Most Fearless series that first brought us on board.” The two journalists also thanked the film’s lead actor Salman Khan, director Apoorva Lakhia and the rest of the team for the opportunity to be associated with the project. They added, “We are grateful to Salman Khan, Apoorva Lakhia and the entire team for their warmth and the opportunity to be part of this journey. We hold them in the highest regard and wish them the very best as they bring their vision to the screen. Our heartfelt wishes for the film’s success will always be with them.” A statement from @RahulSinghx & me, as we wish the Maatrubhumi film team the very best!
@BeingSalmanKhan @LakhiaApoorva @SKFilmsOfficial #IndiasMostFearless — Shiv Aroor (@ShivAroor) November 5, 2026 A project rooted in the Galwan Valley clash
